     sticky(7), symlink(7)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ssttaatt() and ffssttaatt() system calls are expected to conform to ISO/IEC
     9945-1:1990 (“POSIX.1”).  The ffssttaattaatt() system call follows The Open
     Group Extended API Set 2 specification.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ssttaatt() and ffssttaatt() system calls appeared in Version 1 AT&T UNIX.  The
     llssttaatt() system call appeared in 4.2BSD.  The ffssttaattaatt() system call ap‐
     peared in FreeBSD 8.0.

BBUUGGSS
     Applying ffssttaatt() to a socket returns a zeroed buffer, except for the
     blocksize field, and a unique device and inode number.

